# ap_profile_noread.eigs — the C6 control variant.
# Run: eigenscript tests/ap_profile_noread.eigs
#
# The same observed write loop as ap_profile.eigs's `write` variant, in a
# program that contains NO predicate read and NO observer NAME anywhere.
# That difference alone is the measurement: EigenScript#915's write-path
# gate arms PER-INTERPRETER-STATE and monotonically -- `obs_needed` is one flag on
# EigsState -- so a single verdict read anywhere in the program (a dead
# function, a different file, an eagerly-resolved load_file target) arms
# entropy bookkeeping for every assignment in every module. The gate also
# scans the constant pool for bare names, so a string literal "report"
# arms it just as well; this file must stay free of BOTH. That is what
# `file_pin` in tests/test_ap_profile.sh enforces.
#
# This is what an observed write costs when nothing in the program reads a
# verdict, and it is the floor the `write` variant should have been
# measured against all along (GAPS.md G7, EigenScript#1046).
#
# Round 10 published this mechanism as "per-module"; round 11 refuted that
# from the source and the runtime, and round 12 missed this file when it
# corrected the other four.

N is 120000

define run_noread(n) as:
    local u is 0.0
    local w is 0.0
    local q is 0.0
    local th is 0.0
    local i is 0
    loop while i < n:
        u is 280.0 + (sin of (i * 0.01))
        w is 2.0 + (cos of (i * 0.01))
        q is 0.01 * (sin of (i * 0.03))
        th is 0.02 * (cos of (i * 0.02))
        i is i + 1
    print of f"noread {i}"

run_noread of (N)
